        "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Inspired by Exit 8, The Underpass is an anomaly hunting game in which you must remember your surroundings and spot any differences in order to escape the loop.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >At release the game has 30+ anomalies, with an average gameplay length of 30-60 minutes.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Features</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Mouse &amp; Keyboard and Controller support.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Autosave system so you never lose progress.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Anomalies do not repeat until all have been discovered, making completionist runs easier.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Customizable graphics settings, allowing the game to run on a wide variety of PCs.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Accessibility settings like toggle sprint, disabling effects such as motion blur, camera sway, etc.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >No flashing lights, large moving patterns or other photosensitive epilepsy triggers*.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >*If you discover a potential epilepsy trigger or other accessibility issue that I have missed, please let me know via the Steam forums!</p>",
        "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Inspired by Exit 8, The Underpass is an anomaly hunting game in which you must remember your surroundings and spot any differences in order to escape the loop.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >At release the game has 30+ anomalies, with an average gameplay length of 30-60 minutes.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Features</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Mouse &amp; Keyboard and Controller support.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Autosave system so you never lose progress.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Anomalies do not repeat until all have been discovered, making completionist runs easier.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Customizable graphics settings, allowing the game to run on a wide variety of PCs.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Accessibility settings like toggle sprint, disabling effects such as motion blur, camera sway, etc.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >No flashing lights, large moving patterns or other photosensitive epilepsy triggers*.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >*If you discover a potential epilepsy trigger or other accessibility issue that I have missed, please let me know via the Steam forums!</p>",
        "short_description": "Trapped in an endlessly-looping underpass, you must stay alert for changes - large or small - to escape.",
